==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tan(c)kard(e)}}, denoting 'a large tub for carrying liquid', perhaps related to {{der|en|nl|tanckaert}},<ref>{{R:OED}}</ref> meaning the same thing, but both of unknown origin. Meaning "drinking vessel" is first recorded late 15th century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtæŋkɚd/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtæŋkəd/}}
* {{hyph|en|tank|ard}} or {{l|en||tan·kard}}
* {{audio|en|En-ca-tankard.oga|Audio (Canada)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A large [[drinking]] [[vessel]], sometimes of [[pewter]], sometimes with a [[glass]] [[base]], with one [[handle]] and often a [[hinge]]d [[cover]].

